<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aodh Buidhe O'Neill</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1283">1283</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Hugh Boy O'Neill</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aodh Buidhe O'Neill was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tir-eoghain">Tír Eoghain</a> in Ulster in the 13th century, who ruled with the backing of the Anglo-Norman earls of Ulster and was killed in 1283. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clandeboye-oneills">Clann Aodha Buidhe</a>, moved east across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-bann">River Bann</a> in the 14th century and founded the lordship of Clandeboye, which takes its name from him.</p></div>
